---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { store } from '../data/store';
import { url } from '../lib/shop';
---
<Layout title="About" description={`Who runs ${store.name}, how the notebooks are made and where they ship from.`}>
	<div class="wrap page-head">
		<h1>Two people, one long bench.</h1>
		<p>{store.name} is a small bindery in {store.location}. We fold, pierce and sew every notebook by hand.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="wrap about">
		<div class="prose">
			<p>We started sewing notebooks for ourselves in 2019 because the ones we could buy would not stay open. A Coptic stitch fixed that, and a few friends asked for one, then a few of their friends. The bindery is still the two of us, a guillotine older than both of us and a long bench by a north-facing window.</p>
			<h2>How a notebook is made</h2>
			<p>Paper arrives in large sheets and is cut down, folded into signatures and pressed overnight. The next day we pierce the sewing stations with a jig, wrap the covers in bookcloth or linen, and sew. A Coptic A5 takes about forty minutes of sewing; a case-bound journal takes two days because the glue has to dry between steps.</p>
			<h2>What we sell, and what we do not</h2>
			<p>We keep the list short on purpose: a few notebooks, the paper we use ourselves, a walnut tray made by a neighbor and the tools you need to start binding. We do not do custom printing or logos, and we do not sell wholesale yet.</p>
			<h2>Materials</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Paper: acid-free wove and dot grid stock, from a mill that publishes its fiber sources.</li>
				<li>Thread: waxed Irish linen and unwaxed cotton.</li>
				<li>Covers: cotton bookcloth, Belgian linen and 100 percent recycled greyboard.</li>
				<li>Packaging: a paper sleeve and a cardboard mailer, no plastic.</li>
			</ul>
			<p><a href={url('/shop/')}>See what is on the shelf now</a>, or <a href={url('/contact/')}>write to us</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<figure class="plate">
			<img src={url('/products/coptic-a5-notebook.svg')} alt="Our Coptic-stitch A5 notebook with its stitched spine" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
			<figcaption>The Coptic A5, the first notebook we sold.</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
		align-items: start;
	}
	.plate {
		margin: 0;
		position: sticky;
		top: 1.5rem;
	}
	figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.6rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}
	@media (max-width: 52rem) {
		.about {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.plate {
			position: static;
			max-width: 26rem;
		}
	}
</style>
